# Tests

- `node:test` + `playwright-core`; `TEST_BROWSER=chromium|firefox|webkit` (Chromium = system Chrome). `npm run test:all` runs all three.
- Files: `spy` (core behavior + activation oracle), `spa` (framework DOM churn: routes, re-rendered navs, late content,
  hash routers, shadow DOM), `ssr` (+ package exports), `docs` (README/llms.txt/types accuracy). Fixtures in `test/fixtures/`,
  served by `scripts/serve.mjs` with a strict CSP. Site and dev-server tests live in the sibling repo `chapterize-js-site`.
- **Attach listeners before the action** (events, `waitForEvent`, console/CSP collectors before `goto`).
- **Bound every wait** (`until(page, fn, arg, ms)` from `helpers.mjs`; no unbounded `waitForFunction`/`waitForEvent`).
- **Kill stray servers before a full run:** `pkill -f "scripts/(serve|dev).mjs"; fuser -k 8080/tcp`.
- Assert on behavior, not implementation details; collect page errors and CSP violations and assert none.
- Use `Spy` in page code for the global build (defined by `helpers.mjs` from `globalName`), never the literal name.
- A flaky test is a bug: find the race (e.g. a stale `scrollend`, an unfinished browser scroll animation) rather than adding sleeps.
- Report pass/fail per engine; never skip a test to get green.
